Aim
To create an Android application that opens the Mobile Data Settings screen.
Algorithm
1.	Start the application. 
2.	Create a button. 
3.	When the button is clicked, open the Mobile Network Settings screen. 
4.	User can enable or disable mobile data manually. 
5.	Stop the application. 
activity_main.xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<LinearLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent"
    android:gravity="center"
    android:orientation="vertical">

    <Button
        android:id="@+id/btnData"
        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:text="Open Mobile Data Settings" />

</LinearLayout>
MainActivity.kt
package com.example.mobiledatasettings

import android.content.Intent
import android.os.Bundle
import android.provider.Settings
import android.widget.Button
import androidx.appcompat.app.AppCompatActivity

class MainActivity : AppCompatActivity() {

    override fun onCreate(savedInstanceState: Bundle?) {
        super.onCreate(savedInstanceState)
        setContentView(R.layout.activity_main)

        val btnData = findViewById<Button>(R.id.btnData)

        btnData.setOnClickListener {
            startActivity(Intent(Settings.ACTION_WIRELESS_SETTINGS))
        }
    }
}
Output
•	When the button is clicked, the Mobile/Wireless Settings screen opens. 
•	The user can manually turn Mobile Data ON or OFF. 
Result
Thus, the Android application to open the Mobile Data Settings screen was developed and executed successfully.

